Position and antenna alignment

Location accepts latitude from -90 to 90 degrees and longitude from -180 to 180 degrees. North and east are positive; south and west are negative. Altitude is metres. Inputs must be finite; the shared location value does not impose a separate numerical altitude bound. A manual position describes the stationary site used for planning. It is not a measured GPS fix, antenna heading, calibration, no-go policy or physical pointing result.

Altitude reference is either unspecified or an operator-declared mean_sea_level. Selecting mean sea level does not perform a datum conversion, survey or geoid correction. Runtime manual-location binding requires the supported declared reference and exact saved revision in addition to all owner admission checks. An unspecified-reference plan is still a numerical planning result, not an admitted execution input.

The GPS panel keeps measured/replay coordinates separate from manual and effective station coordinates. Use GPS is disabled. Its missing contract covers source identity, fix validity, observation time/freshness and horizontal/altitude references. A reported 3D fix is not sufficient to select it. fresh_replay describes a fixture, not today's live timestamp. The fixed replay observation time is retained in structured output. Incomplete aggregates do not acquire manufactured coordinates or a fabricated final unpublished observation.
Review, save, reload and conflicts

Preview writes a review artifact without changing station settings. Save applies the reviewed revision atomically and records a receipt. Repeating a completed apply returns the same receipt without another generation change. Repeating cancel is also safe. A cancelled preview cannot later apply; make a new preview.

Another saved change or an active managed runner can make a preview conflict. Reload and review again. There is no force override. Station changes mark old plans for revalidation; calculate a new plan before making a new run request. Cancellation is not rollback of a saved change.

A save can complete before its receipt or final durability record fails. The interface reports a partial failure and retains the real saved state. Reload before recovery. If that operation is still current, repeating its apply can recover the receipt without changing coordinates twice. Keep partial artifacts; do not blindly repeat an operation whose physical outcome is uncertain.
Calculate and interpret results

Results uses Start (UTC ISO 8601), NORAD ID, Span (days), Minimum elevation (deg) and Local TLE CSV. UTC input must include an explicit offset, such as 2025-05-16T03:00:00Z; an offset is normalized to UTC. The span is one hour through seven days. Elevation is 0 through 90 degrees. At most 256 opportunities are retained.

The default is historical NOAA 15 data with NORAD ID 25338 and a May 2025 start, not a current orbit. Supplying a local CSV makes its source explicit and leaves the file unchanged. SATGS validates the selected identity, CSV fields, TLE lines and checksums. It does not fetch or refresh TLEs in this path. Use current approved local inputs for actual planning and assess freshness separately.

An opportunity contains rise/set times, azimuths, maximum elevation and whether it is circumpolar. Its plan binds the saved station revision, position, altitude reference and exact TLE input. An empty opportunity list means none were found for those inputs, not that the receiver or PTU failed. A circumpolar entry can omit rise/set fields. Report displays retained plans and operation results.

Export... writes a new private JSON report. Use a new filename in an existing private directory. It never overwrites an existing report. This export is not an RF recording, legacy run directory, database insert or Box upload.
Run and PTU controls

Run offers Plan, Configuration JSON, Runtime bindings JSON, Owner settings, Local TLE CSV, Duration (seconds), Opportunity (1-based) and Execution mode. Review run freezes those inputs with the saved position and revision. Start run is a separate confirmation. These fields are not templates for guessing device or broker identities. Ordinary production owner admission remains empty, so normal live execution is unavailable in this release.

The implemented controlled rehearsal uses real software owners with deliberately controlled transport/serial boundaries and a disposable station. It is not a public bypass for run-start. Software completion, submission history, manager outcome and physical state remain separate. Exit 8 means physical state is indeterminate even when a software operation completed.

Cancel run requests local cancellation of a started run. A request or saved progress record does not prove a currently running process, remote cancellation or physical Stop. run-status before a run starts reports not_started. Cancelling a configuration preview is a different operation from cancelling a run.

PTU has Configuration JSON, Connect, Status, Disconnect, target pan/tilt in degrees, Preview and Move. Stop is also visible in the footer. Live bench admission is closed pending the allocated unit's current-position/Stop contract and reviewed setup binding. These controls do not become available by changing a mode label. Opening the page, connecting or editing numbers never requests a move. Protocol-reported position is not measured arrival; acknowledgements, passive disconnect and local cancellation do not establish physical stopping.
