Original and current workflows

The original M-SEL ground station installs a collection of cooperating services, schedules satellite passes through a broker and runs a hardware/RF-oriented pass procedure. Native SATGS adds a shared saved-workspace workflow for configuration, manual position, local calculation and reviewed runtime requests. It is not a replacement GUI for every original service or command.

This comparison uses the fixed original source revision identified in the maintainer reference. Original command forms below were source reviewed, not executed as part of this documentation work. They can contact brokers, change TLE files, start devices, transmit commands or invoke other programs. Do not run them as tutorial steps.
Read the command notation

In this chapter only, uppercase argument names are descriptions, not runnable values. OLD_CONFIG is the approved original YAML configuration file; OLD_SAT_DB its local satellite CSV; SIGNAL_DB its emission-ID CSV; NORAD_ID a satellite in that database; JOB_ID an ID returned by the original queue; and SECONDS, DAYS and DEGREES have the units named. DOWNLINK_MHZ and UPLINK_MHZ are approved RF frequencies in MHz, not numbers supplied by this guide. SAMPLE_MSPS is the approved RF sample rate in millions of samples per second. LOCALE names an existing pass_finder_locales entry. PIX_ID is a configured sensor ID, PTU_ID is a configured application positioner ID, and SERIAL_PORT is that deployment's assigned operating-system device path. An optional subscriber/client ID of 0 selects all configured application IDs; it is not an instruction to use physical wire address 0. Current PREVIEW_ID, PLAN_ID and REQUEST_ID are full actual returned identities from the selected workspace's JSON. They are not interchangeable with legacy numeric job IDs.
